## Changes Summary

| File | What changed & why |
|------|-------------------|
| `src/service/chat.js` | `addFilesToChat({ chat, files })` is new: it dedupes **when the write runs** and **queues** writes per chat, so every `file_list` update starts from the list the previous one stored. `addFileToChat` now delegates to it (same signature/boolean result). `appendChatFiles` performs the single write and keeps non-store chats in sync. |
| `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` | `onAddFiles()` batches a whole drop into **one** write and `onAddFile()` awaits it (the old call ignored the promise, so its `&&` guard was dead code). `processFilePaths()` replaces the per-file loops of `processMultipleFilePaths` / `processJsonFileList`. `confirmUpload()` awaits the uploaded paths instead of firing `onAddFile` in a `forEach`. `decodeDropText()` prevents a stray `%` in a multi-path payload from aborting the drop. |

## Anti-Patterns avoided
- ❌ **Fire-and-forget mutation of a remote collection** (`chatSvc.addFileToChat(...)` without `await`) — every "add" computed its payload from the same stale snapshot.
- ❌ **N requests for one user gesture** — a drop is one intent, it deserves one write.
- ❌ Trusting `if (asyncFn(...))` — a Promise is always truthy.

## Accessibility checklist
- No visual/interaction change: chips are rendered by the unchanged `ChatFileList`, `drop` feedback (`ring-2 ring-primary`) untouched, keyboard path (`ChatFileSelectorModal`) untouched.
- Feedback after a drop is now complete (all files appear), which is the missing success confirmation for the action.

## Implementation steps
1. Apply `src/service/chat.js` (queue + batch API).
2. Apply `src/components/chat/Chat.vue` (batch drop paths, await writes, safe decode).
3. Verify: drag 3+ files from the file explorer onto the chat area → all 3 chips appear and survive a chat reload; drop 3+ OS files → confirm modal → all uploaded paths added; single-file drops unchanged.

